A||||7||Butter||Paint on my Sleeper is Nasty - Advise||||5||
Z||000000||Butter||05-30-2001||05:03 PM||||Hey Yall,<BR>My brother, what drives the BIG truck, seen me the other day in my Fiero and went to wavin' with his whole arm out the window so's I'd see him in his BIG truck.  He tells me he knowd' it wus me cuz of my black door on my somewhat red car.  I told him I never did see him and I hadn't been drunk in a month of Sundays.  He told me when I got close he jerked his arm in cause the paint looked so bad he didn't want nobody to no I wus his brother.  Well I wus wonderin' why he drove all way up from tin buck 2 to tell me how bad my little car looked.  Said he wanted to help me turn it some colour so's he wouldn't have to disown me like some other brother.  Now, the sun done been a hold of this car bad so I got some real burnt paint. You no, worse than Maryjane fixin' supper when Billyjoe has just left town.  So,  <P>My Queztion is: What is the best way to prep such pitted paint and since the panels to be used are different colours what should one do to ensure matched paint? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||84Bill||05-30-2001||06:28 PM||||Welp ya needs ta start by cleanin the car up proper like. mild soapy water and a sponge would do it I rekon. Then ya need bout a passel of 320 & 220 wet/dry sandin papers and commence with the elbow greasein with the 220 follerd by tha 320 fer the primer when yer near done. use soapy water and dip the paper regularly ta keep it from gettin all gummed up. ya needs ta watch the corners and sharp bends soas not ta scuff off all the paint and make a ridge out of em. Sand er down till all the shine (if there be any) is gone and the paint is a right dull lookin, maybe even showin a bit of primer under tha ole paint. sand tha whole pannel fer ya start sandin the really big dings (pits). Feather it out ( the edges of the pit) bout an inch er two usin a sandin block. then spray on some primer over the erea, this will allow 2 things 1 ya can see the ding a bit better and 2 it will fill the ding just a wee litte bit then sand the primer until ya get her just right. repeat the primein as needed until the ding is gone. For the inside edges I like to us steel wool so I dont "burn" off all the paint and start eating at the plastic under pinnins. By the time yer done the pannel will look like a hellin but she'll be right smoothed out( no dings). Shoot the whole pannel with good primer and wet sand it with the 320 nice and smooth, and that pannel is ready fer colorin.<P>Do a panel at a time and befer ya ken kill 3 kegs of beer and maryjane catchin that pig fer supper she'll right rady ta shoot.<P>After yer all done and ya see that big ole honkin truk yer brother drives be sure to fully extend the international hello symbol in the fully extended position, be sure to bring it around in a half circle as he passes by so as it can be properly seen from all possible viewing points.<P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-30-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000002||grinthock||05-30-2001||06:38 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   Cute bill||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroHarry||05-30-2001||06:42 PM||||Ya'll makin fun at uss rednecks,<BR>me-n-billy be rit ovr to pull ur valve stems off. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||05-30-2001||06:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroHarry:<BR><B>Ya'll makin fun at uss rednecks,<BR>me-n-billy be rit ovr to pull ur valve stems off.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>LOL!<BR>Naw I lived in florida for 8 years I had a bit of a draw when I got back to Pa but I used all the suthun slang like "fixen" and "yalls" ect  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Butter||06-01-2001||10:12 AM||||84Bill,<BR>U aw ite.  What u thank I ouhta do bout taht deep fried paint what is on top of da car?Some of the paint appears to be damaged past the original primer.  I would have ansered back for now but somebody's got to work around here.||||reg||10
Z||000006||84Bill||06-01-2001||11:25 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Butter:<BR><B>84Bill,<BR>U aw ite.  What u thank I ouhta do bout taht deep fried paint what is on top of da car?Some of the paint appears to be damaged past the original primer.  I would have ansered back for now but somebody's got to work around here.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah I'm ok buba buttuh   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> havin a bit of fun thats all. There is no way you can save the original paint if it's burnt as bad as you say. Only a repaint will save it. You can get the paint code off the the sticker on the left front wheel well under the front hood.<BR>If you look at bottom of the picture you can see the Paint code for my car, I have 2 sets of numbers WA-8554-7719. The paint codes start with WA- <BR>If it's an 84 then there will be a metal plate on the same side on the inside front of the tire well.<P>When you get your code look it up here <A HREF="http://www.paintscratch.com/search.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.paintscratch.com/search.htm</A> <P>  <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Indy/image0110.jpg">  <P>To prep the car to repaint it, Just clean the car with soapy water so you dont go grinding dirt into the surface and scratch the hell out of it. then wet sand it with 220 paper. Prime it then wet sand the primer with 320 when it dries. This will give a good surface for the paint to stick to. Then just paint on a color you like.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-01-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000007||rogergarrison||06-01-2001||06:10 PM||||easier way and faster is the way American Motors did it. get a big tub of paint and just dip the whole car in it.||||reg||1
